{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>בetter a meal of</b> — It stands in place of two words, on account of one who hosts a guest, like <b>שלוחים</b> from ישלח and <b>מנחה</b> from נחה. The noun refers to the hosted meal — meaning that they love one another — better than a fatted ox, and they hate one another."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:59.492337351Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}